Xorn are fun -- you can still wield a weapon and you can travel through
rock.  You can eat metal rings and gain intrinsics from them.  Dragons
(particularly grey and black) are quite powerful.  I don't know if you can 
survive polymorphing into a cockatrice, but if you could you'd be the
terror of the dungeons.  If you change into a tengu, you might be able to 
teleport at will -- I've never tried this, so I don't know.  If you have
the spoilers at hand, look at the monster lists and see which ones are
the most powerful, then experiment.  

Three warnings, though:  1) you can't change into certain super-monsters
like an Archon or Medusa.  2) if you change into a non-humanoid critter,
you'll either destroy your armor when you rip out of it or you'll have
to drop it all, depending on how big or small you get.  3) You will change
back into a human sometimes without being given the option of polymorphing.
This can be a problem (i.e. you're a xorn careening around the screen
when suddenly you turn back into a human and you're stuck in
the rock.)

